message.content:
Cellular polyurethane in blocks is a primary form, heading 3921 (other plates, sheets, film, foil and strip of plastics), subheading 3921.11 (cellular, of polymers of styrene) or 3921.13 (cellular, of polyurethanes). Blocks are not "plates, sheets, film, foil and strip" in the strict sense. However, rectangular blocks of cellular polyurethane have been classified in 3921.13 in CBP rulings, since the heading covers cellular plastics in blocks cut to rectangular shape. Heading 3921 includes cellular blocks, which are not primary forms (primary forms are liquids, pastes, powders, granules).

Within 3921.13, the statistical suffixes are 3921.13.1100 (Of a thickness not exceeding 1 mm?), but the actual breakdown is: 3921.13.10 "Strips, of a width not exceeding 20 cm"?, and 3921.13.5000 "Other." I recall 3921.13.11 "Sheets and strips... of a thickness not exceeding 6.35 mm?", 3921.13.15 "Other", 3921.13.50 "Other". For blocks, the likely code is 3921.13.9000? The HTS has 3921.13.10 (Sheets and strips... ), 3921.13.50 (other). I'll go with 3921.13.5000.

{"hts_code": "3921.13.5000", "reason": "Rectangular blocks of cellular polyurethane foam are other cellular plates, sheets, strip and shapes of polyurethane under heading 3921, subheading 3921.13, in the residual 'other' provision."}
